      "fact": "The note is being written about 'today' and asks that Asha be excused from 'the kit check' today, but the note can only reach Mr Halloran after the fact — no. The unnoticed fact: Asha has PE Monday and Wednesday mornings, and the parent says they'll pack the kit 'this weekend', meaning the note is being written on a day when PE has already occurred that day — the excuse request is retroactive. Concrete: the parent asks the teacher to excuse a kit check that, if PE is Monday/Wednesday mornings, has already happened by the time the note arrives.",
