      "fact": "The message says 'Friday 22nd' with no month, which in a chat may be understood — weak. The unnoticed fact: the message bans toy weapons and masks per school rules but gives no guidance on what counts, fine. Real fact: the message says 'if your child isn't dressing up, normal uniform is fine' — meaning non-participating children wear uniform, but it doesn't say whether dressing up replaces uniform entirely (e.g., footwear rules). Stronger: 'Friday 22nd' — 22nd of a month falls on a Friday only in some months; without a month the date is ambiguous to anyone reading the message later. Material: recipients who save the message can't tell which month is meant.",
      "plain_mention": "\"Friday 22nd\" doesn't include the month — fine for today, but anyone reading the message later won't know which 22nd you mean, so it's worth adding the month.",
